@Tutorial {
  @Intro(title: "Getting started") {
    From an empty machine to a running reader in six steps. Run them in an interactive shell: two of
    the commands prompt for passwords on the terminal and do not work from a pipe or a service unit.
  }

  @Section(title: "Set up and run") {
    The first steps create the database and the account, then add a feed, and the last starts the
    server.

    @Steps {
      @Step {
        Point Rivulet at its database: set `DATABASE_URL` to a path such as
        `/var/lib/rivulet/rivulet.db`. It is the only required setting.
      }

      @Step {
        Create the schema with `rivulet migrate`. Running it again on a current database does
        nothing.
      }

      @Step {
        Create the account with `rivulet create-admin`, then the logins your apps use with
        `rivulet integration-credentials` (a Fever pair and a Google Reader pair). Until the second
        command has run, app logins answer 401.
      }

      @Step {
        Subscribe to a feed with `rivulet add https://example.com/feed.xml --user alice`. The feed is
        fetched on the server's next scheduler pass, or right away with `rivulet refresh`.
      }

      @Step {
        Check the state with `rivulet status --json`, then start the server with `rivulet serve`. It
        listens on `LISTEN_ADDR` and refreshes feeds in the background.
      }

      @Step {
        Take a backup with `rivulet backup --verify /var/backups/rivulet.db`, which writes a
        consistent copy and checks its integrity.
      }
    }
  }
}
